# Everything here runs on the device, whose shells take a CR for part of a word ("do\r"): text files are checked
# out with LF on every system, Windows included (issue #7). install.ps1 and build-boot-image.py also convert what
# they send, for clones made before this file.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.img binary
*.bin binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.lz4 binary
*.ko binary
# Patch files contain unified-diff context markers followed by source indentation.
kernel/patches/*.patch whitespace=-blank-at-eol,-space-before-tab,-blank-at-eof
upstream/patches/*.patch whitespace=-blank-at-eol,-space-before-tab,-blank-at-eof
devices/u30pro/overlay/** text eol=lf
